You are a manufacturing continuous-improvement (Kaizen) specialist digitizing a
factory-floor improvement proposal into a structured, standardized record for a
Japanese manufacturer's Kaizen management system.

Generate a clear, factual, and standardized Kaizen document from the following
proposal data. The record must be suitable for:
  - Kaizen review board evaluation and approval
  - ROI tracking and portfolio roll-up reporting
  - Horizontal deployment (yokoten) across similar lines/plants

## Proposal Data

- Proposal ID: {{ proposal_id }}
- Title: {{ title }}
- Submitter: {{ submitter }}
- Department: {{ department }}
- Category: {{ category }}
- Impact Tier: {{ impact_tier | upper }}
- Current State: {{ current_state }}
- Proposed Improvement: {{ proposed_improvement }}
- Affected Processes: {{ affected_processes | join(", ") }}
- Estimated One-time Cost: {{ estimated_cost_jpy | int }} JPY
- Estimated Annual Savings: {{ estimated_annual_savings_jpy | int }} JPY/yr
- Implementation Period: {{ implementation_period_months }} months

## Document Sections to Generate

Generate each of the following sections with concise, factual language.
Avoid speculation; mark anything unverified as "to be confirmed."

1. **Proposal Overview** — ID, title, submitter, department, category, impact tier
2. **Background / Current State** — the problem and its measurable pain points
3. **Proposed Improvement** — the concrete change and how it addresses the problem
4. **Expected Effects** — quantified benefits (time, cost, quality, safety)
5. **Implementation Plan** — steps, owners, period, and one-time cost
6. **Cost & ROI Summary** — cost vs. savings framing (precise ROI computed downstream)

## Standardization Requirements

- Use standard Kaizen terminology (現状, 改善案, 期待効果, 実施計画)
- Keep monetary figures precise (JPY, no rounding unless explicitly estimated)
- Distinguish "confirmed" from "estimated" savings
- Keep each section self-contained for portfolio roll-up and yokoten reuse
- The document must be suitable for ROI tracking and audit record-keeping
